WEBVTT

1
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:50.468
Tal'Dorei's kingdoms
lay broken at my feet.

2
00:00:50.551 --> 00:00:53.971
yet my conclave continues to fail me.

3
00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.890
Send me. my king.

4
00:00:55.973 --> 00:00:58.642
I will dispatch those that threaten you.

5
00:00:58.726 --> 00:01:00.686
You have your talents.

6
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.063
But with Umbrasyl fallen.

7
00:01:03.147 --> 00:01:07.276
Raishan's mission
is more crucial than ever.

8
00:01:10.196 --> 00:01:11.697
We are not alone.

9
00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:21.832
Something was here.

10
00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:36.806
What?

11
00:01:41.435 --> 00:01:42.978
Oh. gods.

12
00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:45.356
Yes.

13
00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:49.151
My children soon will be gods.

14
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.064
No!

15
00:02:38.242 --> 00:02:40.202
{\an8}<i>Thordak is becoming irrational.</i>

16
00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:41.787
{\an8}<i>Insane.</i>

17
00:02:41.871 --> 00:02:44.957
Intent on stripping Tal'Dorei of its gold.

18
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:47.835
But not to satisfy his greed.

19
00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:49.837
For another purpose.

20
00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.422
What purpose?

21
00:02:52.673 --> 00:02:54.800
- Enough of this yappin'!
- Grog. don't!

22
00:02:57.595 --> 00:02:58.637
Okay.

23
00:02:58.721 --> 00:03:00.180
Maybe a little more yappin'.

24
00:03:00.264 --> 00:03:03.976
Everyone in this chamber shares a goal.

25
00:03:04.059 --> 00:03:06.020
The end of the Cinder King.

26
00:03:06.103 --> 00:03:10.065
And if you join me. it is a goal
we are capable of achieving.

27
00:03:10.149 --> 00:03:13.319
We know firsthand what you're capable of.

28
00:03:13.402 --> 00:03:15.613
Your kind razed Byroden.

29
00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:18.282
Nearly everyone in our village dead.

30
00:03:18.365 --> 00:03:20.075
Including our mother.

31
00:03:20.159 --> 00:03:22.703
Not all dragons are the same.

32
00:03:22.786 --> 00:03:26.123
Some can be cruel.

33
00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:29.168
Some can be clever.

34
00:03:29.251 --> 00:03:31.712
But some can be truthful.

35
00:03:37.009 --> 00:03:40.179
Thordak did that to you?

36
00:03:40.262 --> 00:03:41.805
Not exactly.

37
00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:44.308
But he will be punished nonetheless.

38
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:46.644
So it's revenge you're after.

39
00:03:46.727 --> 00:03:49.897
Not a stranger to vengeance. are you?

40
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.984
Then you know
it can create unusual allies.

41
00:03:54.068 --> 00:03:55.569
So what did he do to you?

42
00:03:55.653 --> 00:03:57.446
Lovers' quarrel?

43
00:03:57.529 --> 00:04:00.491
It's not what Thordak did.

44
00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:03.094
<i>It's what he didn't do.</i>

45
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.580
<i>Trapped in the Fire Plane.</i>

46
00:04:06.664 --> 00:04:08.582
<i>tethered to the soul anchor.</i>

47
00:04:08.666 --> 00:04:12.127
<i>Thordak was a pathetic prisoner of flame.</i>

48
00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:20.886
<i>Until I snuck through Pyrah
to strike a deal with him.</i>

49
00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.597
<i>A runic curse afflicts me.</i>

50
00:04:23.681 --> 00:04:28.978
<i>But centuries of survival
have given Thordak knowledge of a cure.</i>

51
00:04:29.061 --> 00:04:32.564
Free me. diseased deceiver.

52
00:04:32.648 --> 00:04:35.609
and I shall free you of your ailment.

53
00:04:37.027 --> 00:04:40.531
<i>The bonds of the soul anchor
were unbreakable.</i>

54
00:04:40.614 --> 00:04:42.491
<i>But with my magic.</i>

55
00:04:42.574 --> 00:04:44.243
<i>he gave himself over to it.</i>

56
00:04:44.326 --> 00:04:46.161
<i>Fused with it.</i>

57
00:04:46.245 --> 00:04:49.248
<i>Its elemental force nourishing his body.</i>

58
00:04:49.331 --> 00:04:52.001
<i>contaminating his mind.</i>

59
00:05:01.301 --> 00:05:04.263
<i>I begged him to use prudence.</i>

60
00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:09.852
<i>But the gem gave him ungodly power.</i>

61
00:05:14.773 --> 00:05:17.401
<i>And uncontrollable rage.</i>

62
00:05:23.532 --> 00:05:25.367
He called himself king.

63
00:05:25.451 --> 00:05:27.745
Demanded I find loyal subjects.

64
00:05:27.828 --> 00:05:29.496
His conclave.

65
00:05:30.581 --> 00:05:31.749
And the cure?

66
00:05:31.832 --> 00:05:33.792
There is no cure.

67
00:05:33.876 --> 00:05:35.711
Then why not slay him yourself?

68
00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:38.088
Your magic made him like this.

69
00:05:38.172 --> 00:05:42.051
With that crystal in his chest.
neither of us can destroy him alone.

70
00:05:42.134 --> 00:05:43.302
But together...

71
00:05:43.385 --> 00:05:45.095
There is no "together." bitch.

72
00:05:45.179 --> 00:05:46.722
You opened that rift.

73
00:05:46.805 --> 00:05:49.558
Half of Pyrah is dead because of you.

74
00:05:49.641 --> 00:05:51.727
I freed him. yes.

75
00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.229
He massacred your people. true.

76
00:05:54.313 --> 00:05:57.316
I assume you wish me dead. Ashari?

77
00:05:57.399 --> 00:05:58.984
That's an understatement.

78
00:05:59.068 --> 00:06:01.320
Your wish will soon be granted.

79
00:06:01.403 --> 00:06:03.572
The pain grows worse every day.

80
00:06:03.655 --> 00:06:06.784
But I will see Thordak pay for his lies

81
00:06:06.867 --> 00:06:08.827
before his plan comes to fruition.

82
00:06:08.911 --> 00:06:12.122
Plan. plan... What plan?
This vague bullshit's getting old.

83
00:06:12.206 --> 00:06:16.877
A new order of elemental dragons
born of his own spawn.

84
00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:20.130
When his brood of eggs in Emon hatches.

85
00:06:20.214 --> 00:06:22.800
your world will be bathed in fire.

86
00:06:28.889 --> 00:06:30.516
My vision.

87
00:06:30.599 --> 00:06:32.559
When will these eggs hatch?

88
00:06:32.643 --> 00:06:34.686
Weeks. Maybe days.

89
00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:38.148
I mean. what are we waitin' for?
We got vesticles...

90
00:06:38.232 --> 00:06:41.193
- Vestiges.
- They whupped Umbrasyl.

91
00:06:41.276 --> 00:06:42.861
Let's charge that castle

92
00:06:42.945 --> 00:06:44.696
- and whup him. too!
- Ha.

93
00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.825
You'd be destroyed in a heartbeat.

94
00:06:47.908 --> 00:06:52.371
You may have vestiges
but not the one you need.

95
00:06:52.454 --> 00:06:54.623
The Plate of the Dawnmartyr.

96
00:06:54.706 --> 00:06:58.418
Magical armor
that can repel hellfire itself.

97
00:06:58.502 --> 00:07:00.504
It has felled dragons before.

98
00:07:03.132 --> 00:07:05.551
And it can again.

99
00:07:07.970 --> 00:07:09.810
I don't suppose you brought
this thing with you

100
00:07:09.888 --> 00:07:11.974
in. like. a big purse or. like. a tote?

101
00:07:12.057 --> 00:07:13.851
It resides in Ank'Harel.

102
00:07:13.934 --> 00:07:17.229
Located by Umbrasyl
before you destroyed him.

103
00:07:17.312 --> 00:07:19.815
Now another treasure hunter seeks it.

104
00:07:19.898 --> 00:07:22.151
So time is of the essence.

105
00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:25.320
Raishan. go fuck yourself.

106
00:07:25.404 --> 00:07:27.823
Anyone can conjure illusions.

107
00:07:27.906 --> 00:07:29.366
This is clearly an ambush.

108
00:07:29.449 --> 00:07:31.785
And we are not falling for it.

109
00:07:31.869 --> 00:07:33.328
The answer is no.

110
00:07:33.412 --> 00:07:36.081
You all agree with the Ashari?

111
00:07:36.165 --> 00:07:37.499
We're a team.

112
00:07:40.043 --> 00:07:42.880
Without an alliance. I die.

113
00:07:42.963 --> 00:07:44.715
As do you.

114
00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:48.260
But if that's the path you've chosen...

115
00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:49.636
No. no. don't let her do it.

116
00:07:55.058 --> 00:07:56.185
Kima.

117
00:07:56.268 --> 00:07:57.936
Shaun.

118
00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.229
Are you all right?

119
00:07:59.313 --> 00:08:01.231
Waking in your arms again?

120
00:08:01.315 --> 00:08:03.859
Oh. you should start charging me.

121
00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:08.197
Ow.

122
00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.116
For the last time. Grog. it's me.

123
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.202
Mm-hmm. Well. then say something

124
00:08:13.285 --> 00:08:16.038
only the real Keeper Yennen would know.

125
00:08:17.206 --> 00:08:20.375
Sometimes you wear a crown
and call yourself

126
00:08:20.459 --> 00:08:23.712
"Grand Poo-bah de Mayonnaise"
when no one's looking.

127
00:08:24.796 --> 00:08:26.506
Yeah. okay. it's her.

128
00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.967
Thank the Dawnfather
she only locked you in the dungeon.

129
00:08:29.051 --> 00:08:30.636
It could have been far worse.

130
00:08:30.719 --> 00:08:32.221
The question remains.

131
00:08:32.304 --> 00:08:34.848
Do we dare chase down this armor?

132
00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:36.433
Conspire with Raishan?

133
00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:37.851
No way.

134
00:08:37.935 --> 00:08:39.645
She killed Sovereign Uriel.

135
00:08:39.728 --> 00:08:41.021
It's a deal with a devil.

136
00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:42.522
But how badass would it be

137
00:08:42.606 --> 00:08:45.067
if we rolled in riding a fucking dragon?

138
00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.486
Knock-knock. Thordak! Acid!

139
00:08:47.569 --> 00:08:48.904
Uh. she shoots poison.

140
00:08:48.987 --> 00:08:49.988
Oh. Right.

141
00:08:50.072 --> 00:08:51.657
Knock-knock. Thordak!

142
00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:53.242
Poison!

143
00:08:53.325 --> 00:08:56.078
If she helps defeat the conclave.
that's well worth it.

144
00:08:56.161 --> 00:08:59.957
I don't like this. either.
but Raishan could have just attacked us.

145
00:09:00.040 --> 00:09:01.792
She wanted to talk.

146
00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:03.377
Maybe we should listen.

147
00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:05.003
To a mass murderer?

148
00:09:05.087 --> 00:09:08.799
Sometimes a stiff moral code
must be bent for the greater good.

149
00:09:08.882 --> 00:09:09.883
No!

150
00:09:09.967 --> 00:09:12.678
I will not dishonor the Ashari.

151
00:09:16.932 --> 00:09:19.476
I'll go after her.

152
00:09:21.937 --> 00:09:24.356
So. we all going out the window?

153
00:09:34.199 --> 00:09:35.617
Whoever's there.

154
00:09:35.701 --> 00:09:37.869
you don't want to fuck with me tonight.

155
00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:40.497
I don't doubt it.

156
00:09:42.916 --> 00:09:47.004
The idea of working with that monster.

157
00:09:47.087 --> 00:09:48.672
After what she did to my people.

158
00:09:48.755 --> 00:09:49.756
I know.

159
00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:53.260
And the rest of the team.

160
00:09:53.343 --> 00:09:55.804
It always feels like
my opinions don't count.

161
00:09:55.887 --> 00:09:57.347
They count with me.

162
00:09:57.431 --> 00:09:59.057
Do they. Vax?

163
00:09:59.141 --> 00:10:01.810
Y-You've been so...

164
00:10:01.893 --> 00:10:03.061
different.

165
00:10:03.145 --> 00:10:04.479
I miss you.

166
00:10:04.563 --> 00:10:07.691
There were things I needed to understand.

167
00:10:07.774 --> 00:10:08.859
With the Matron.

168
00:10:08.942 --> 00:10:10.527
And do you?

169
00:10:11.611 --> 00:10:14.573
Not everything. But enough.

170
00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:16.450
There's a balance.

171
00:10:16.533 --> 00:10:19.161
Like I'm finally ready for...

172
00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:21.330
whatever comes next.

173
00:10:25.125 --> 00:10:28.045
I'm glad you have someone
who supports you.

174
00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:30.589
Kiki.

175
00:10:31.798 --> 00:10:34.384
I can be that person for you.

176
00:10:34.468 --> 00:10:35.969
if you need me to.

177
00:10:37.804 --> 00:10:41.308
I need that a lot right now.

178
00:11:04.748 --> 00:11:07.084
Sorry. Sorry. Was that bad?

179
00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:09.044
I-I felt your tongue.
and it freaked me out.

180
00:11:09.127 --> 00:11:11.838
and-and I'm-I'm new at this and...

181
00:11:11.922 --> 00:11:15.592
No. no. it was wonderful.

182
00:11:15.675 --> 00:11:18.720
Just... intense.

183
00:11:18.804 --> 00:11:22.140
And. um. I-I need a moment.

184
00:11:22.224 --> 00:11:24.184
Oh. um. okay.

185
00:11:24.267 --> 00:11:26.812
I'll walk back first. then.

186
00:11:26.895 --> 00:11:28.897
so no one suspects.

187
00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:30.857
I'll see you there.

188
00:11:41.368 --> 00:11:43.120
You're up early.

189
00:11:43.203 --> 00:11:45.664
Never slept. I hate our options.

190
00:11:45.747 --> 00:11:49.334
And I hate how it's driving a wedge
between the group.

191
00:11:49.418 --> 00:11:51.253
Bollocks.

192
00:11:51.336 --> 00:11:54.172
What's really bothering you. darling?

193
00:11:56.341 --> 00:11:59.261
When the Briarwoods came.

194
00:11:59.344 --> 00:12:01.763
no one could have prevented it.

195
00:12:01.847 --> 00:12:04.850
But this... I did this.

196
00:12:04.933 --> 00:12:09.020
I had us flee here. and Raishan followed.

197
00:12:09.104 --> 00:12:11.523
I've endangered my people once more.

198
00:12:11.606 --> 00:12:15.110
The way you self-analyze.
I've always admired it.

199
00:12:15.193 --> 00:12:18.613
But at some point.
you have to forgive yourself.

200
00:12:18.697 --> 00:12:20.949
No one can undo the past.

201
00:12:21.032 --> 00:12:23.285
Well. one can certainly try.

202
00:12:24.286 --> 00:12:27.164
You may know me better
than I know myself. Vex'ahlia.

203
00:12:27.247 --> 00:12:31.751
And you're right. I must focus
on the problems ahead.

204
00:12:31.835 --> 00:12:33.920
On fixing this.

205
00:12:34.004 --> 00:12:35.589
Well. not this. This is rubbish.

206
00:12:35.672 --> 00:12:38.341
I know we can.

207
00:12:38.425 --> 00:12:40.051
Together.

208
00:12:42.179 --> 00:12:44.097
Hmm.

209
00:12:45.807 --> 00:12:47.934
Right.

210
00:12:48.018 --> 00:12:51.771
I was thinking. it won't matter
whether Raishan is lying

211
00:12:51.855 --> 00:12:53.940
if we can get to those eggs.

212
00:12:54.024 --> 00:12:57.277
If they're real. we'd have an ally.

213
00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.528
And if they aren't...

214
00:12:58.612 --> 00:13:01.406
Then we let our vestiges do the talking.

215
00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:03.700
Shall we wake the others?

216
00:13:03.783 --> 00:13:05.994
Trinket?

217
00:13:11.291 --> 00:13:15.212
Sun Tree. if you can hear me.
grant us luck.

218
00:13:20.842 --> 00:13:23.678
A stealth mission
into a dragon's lair.

219
00:13:23.762 --> 00:13:26.640
You've come a long way
from stealing from my shop.

220
00:13:26.723 --> 00:13:28.725
my handsome half-elf.

221
00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:31.937
Ah. you know. Same game. bigger walls.

222
00:13:32.020 --> 00:13:33.980
The item you requested.

223
00:13:35.065 --> 00:13:36.525
Should make quite a show.

224
00:13:36.608 --> 00:13:39.194
I'd expect nothing less. Shaun.

225
00:13:39.277 --> 00:13:41.029
This feels weird every time.

226
00:13:41.112 --> 00:13:43.365
Hmm.

227
00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.792
Whoa. Place looks like shit.

228
00:13:55.877 --> 00:13:58.255
Good to be home.

229
00:14:01.299 --> 00:14:03.176
All right. huddle up.

230
00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:07.138
As we know. I'll be making
a daring aerial incursion.

231
00:14:07.222 --> 00:14:08.640
Which is certain to fail.

232
00:14:08.723 --> 00:14:10.308
I mean. I wouldn't say "certain."

233
00:14:10.392 --> 00:14:12.644
Is highly likely to fail.

234
00:14:12.727 --> 00:14:15.063
I'm sort of with Vex on this one.

235
00:14:16.147 --> 00:14:17.774
Thank you. Stubby.

236
00:14:17.857 --> 00:14:20.527
In any case. you all have
your backup assignments.

237
00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:21.736
Yep.

238
00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:23.947
<i>I'm on rock duty.</i>

239
00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:26.950
<i>Me and Grog will get
up close and personal with our vestiges.</i>

240
00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:28.118
<i>Vesticles.</i>

241
00:14:28.201 --> 00:14:30.120
<i>With mine circling overhead.</i>

242
00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:32.581
<i>I'll be watching Vax.</i>

243
00:14:32.664 --> 00:14:35.667
<i>And I'll be ready
with the signal for when he fails.</i>

244
00:14:35.750 --> 00:14:38.461
If. If I fail.

245
00:14:38.545 --> 00:14:40.297
Sure. brother. Sure.

246
00:14:41.339 --> 00:14:43.592
Plan sounds aces.

247
00:14:43.675 --> 00:14:45.677
What could possibly go wrong?

248
00:14:51.725 --> 00:14:53.810
No!

249
00:15:09.326 --> 00:15:11.161
Shit. shit. Do the thing!

250
00:15:19.377 --> 00:15:22.172
Let's give him a taste of our toys!

251
00:15:24.341 --> 00:15:26.885
<i>♪ Mythcarver ho! ♪</i>

252
00:15:26.968 --> 00:15:28.928
More insects.

253
00:15:29.012 --> 00:15:31.681
Oh. fuck!

254
00:15:35.435 --> 00:15:38.104
A bigger target.

255
00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:03.922
Oi! Thordak!

256
00:16:12.847 --> 00:16:15.225
Come on. We need to rejoin the fight.

257
00:16:15.308 --> 00:16:16.851
No. damn it.

258
00:16:16.935 --> 00:16:18.687
She was right about all of it.

259
00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.397
The eggs. the nest.

260
00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:22.482
The vestiges aren't enough.

261
00:16:22.565 --> 00:16:24.234
We need to run.

262
00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.707
These are the vestiges
Umbrasyl coveted?

263
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:43.294
Your relics will lie in ash
with your corpses.

264
00:16:45.046 --> 00:16:46.673
Go! Take cover!

265
00:16:54.764 --> 00:16:55.849
Pike!

266
00:17:03.189 --> 00:17:05.275
We need to hide! Now!

267
00:17:07.277 --> 00:17:08.695
Quickly! In there!

268
00:17:19.664 --> 00:17:21.833
Can't run. can't hide. What do we do?

269
00:17:21.916 --> 00:17:23.251
The arrogance!

270
00:17:23.334 --> 00:17:26.463
That you would dare enter my domain?

271
00:17:32.385 --> 00:17:35.764
- Raishan?
- Careful where you point that.

272
00:17:35.847 --> 00:17:37.265
This is your fault.

273
00:17:37.348 --> 00:17:38.808
You told Thordak we were coming.

274
00:17:38.892 --> 00:17:41.394
Fool. I warned you.

275
00:17:41.478 --> 00:17:44.439
Get us out of here. and we'll reconsider.

276
00:17:44.522 --> 00:17:46.566
Finally. a rational mind.

277
00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.491
Come close.

278
00:17:55.867 --> 00:17:57.535
Group hug. Everybody get intimate.

279
00:18:14.594 --> 00:18:16.513
Somebody put out that fire.

280
00:18:16.596 --> 00:18:18.139
I gotcha. Just... Aah!

281
00:18:19.516 --> 00:18:21.142
Kiki...

282
00:18:28.441 --> 00:18:30.902
Hold still. Try not to move.

283
00:18:33.321 --> 00:18:34.948
Now do you trust me?

284
00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:39.869
Then make haste for Ank'Harel.

285
00:18:51.047 --> 00:18:53.466
You're safe. my progeny.

286
00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:55.093
Safe.

287
00:18:55.176 --> 00:18:56.761
But how did they get that close?

288
00:18:58.638 --> 00:19:00.849
No. it's all right. Shh.

289
00:19:00.932 --> 00:19:02.725
It won't happen again.

290
00:19:02.809 --> 00:19:06.229
For I will have Vox Machina brought to me.

291
00:19:06.312 --> 00:19:10.400
and they shall burn.

292
00:19:38.344 --> 00:19:41.014
{\an8}Ank'Harel. the Jewel of Marquet.

293
00:19:41.097 --> 00:19:44.058
{\an8}Also. fun fact.
my old stomping grounds.

294
00:19:44.142 --> 00:19:47.353
Over here is the famed Suncut Bazaar.

295
00:19:47.437 --> 00:19:50.356
The River District. where you can find
anything your heart desires.

296
00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:51.816
And I do mean anything.

297
00:19:52.901 --> 00:19:54.068
<i>Ah.</i>

298
00:19:54.152 --> 00:19:57.322
<i>Those fearsome men in uniform
are the Hand of Ord.</i>

299
00:19:57.405 --> 00:20:02.160
<i>Guardians of the mysterious emperex
of this place. J'mon Sa Ord.</i>

300
00:20:04.454 --> 00:20:07.415
<i>And down this street is where
your dragon friend said</i>

301
00:20:07.498 --> 00:20:09.918
<i>we'd find the vestige.</i>

302
00:20:10.001 --> 00:20:14.130
I. uh. don't suppose you want to break in
and steal a priceless relic for us?

303
00:20:14.213 --> 00:20:16.966
Mm. I'm a salesman now. friend.

304
00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:20.261
All your palace intrigue.
no longer intriguing.

305
00:20:20.345 --> 00:20:24.223
If you need me. I'll be sipping
a glass of Stassman down the street.

306
00:20:24.307 --> 00:20:25.516
Ta-ta.

307
00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:27.727
Hey. uh. Gil. if a fella were looking for

308
00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:29.854
a traveling musical act around here.

309
00:20:29.938 --> 00:20:31.648
where would he start?

310
00:20:31.731 --> 00:20:33.775
Where do you think you're going?

311
00:20:33.858 --> 00:20:36.945
Vex. remember that favor you owe me?

312
00:20:40.031 --> 00:20:41.574
All right. we know the drill.

313
00:20:41.658 --> 00:20:43.660
Simple smash-and-grab. Home by supper.

314
00:20:43.743 --> 00:20:45.328
Easier said than done.

315
00:20:45.411 --> 00:20:47.747
It's high noon. There are eyes everywhere.

316
00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.707
Then we call it off.

317
00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.376
What?

318
00:20:51.459 --> 00:20:54.879
Raishan's holding all the cards.
and we're exactly where she wants us.

319
00:20:55.964 --> 00:20:57.715
Vax?

320
00:20:57.799 --> 00:21:00.301
What other play do we have?

321
00:21:00.385 --> 00:21:02.178
I-I don't know.

322
00:21:02.261 --> 00:21:04.555
But I refuse to believe
that our only two choices

323
00:21:04.639 --> 00:21:06.182
are Raishan or failure.

324
00:21:06.265 --> 00:21:08.434
Keyleth. I...

325
00:21:09.727 --> 00:21:12.772
Percy? That sounded like...

326
00:21:36.462 --> 00:21:39.716
We're not the only ones
who want that plate.

327
00:21:43.261 --> 00:21:44.595
These wounds.

328
00:21:44.679 --> 00:21:47.807
Hey. Stay with me. Who did this to you?

329
00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:51.102
She is still here.

330
00:22:04.032 --> 00:22:06.743
A pepperbox. It can't be.

331
00:22:06.826 --> 00:22:09.662
Percy. we need to keep our heads
if we're going to...

332
00:22:09.746 --> 00:22:11.789
- Right behind you. Percy!
- Wait!

333
00:22:33.728 --> 00:22:35.980
Everyone. get down!

334
00:22:40.234 --> 00:22:41.402
Sorry.

335
00:22:41.486 --> 00:22:42.737
I'll try to stabilize him.

336
00:22:44.155 --> 00:22:46.449
Vex. your broom. Follow them.

337
00:22:46.532 --> 00:22:48.993
I... I gave it to Scanlan.

338
00:22:49.077 --> 00:22:50.161
You what?!

339
00:23:18.439 --> 00:23:20.858
Vax. look out!

340
00:23:20.942 --> 00:23:22.610
Ah. shit. Sorry.

341
00:23:51.597 --> 00:23:52.598
Spice?

342
00:23:52.682 --> 00:23:53.975
Aah! Uh. I'm sorry. what?

343
00:23:54.058 --> 00:23:56.352
You spice? Spice it?

344
00:23:56.435 --> 00:23:57.770
What? Oh.

345
00:23:57.854 --> 00:23:59.438
Uh. I mean. sometime...

346
00:23:59.522 --> 00:24:01.774
No. no. not right now. I'm...

347
00:24:01.858 --> 00:24:03.234
I'm going to see my daughter.

348
00:24:03.317 --> 00:24:05.361
Oh.

349
00:24:05.444 --> 00:24:07.029
Does she spice?

350
00:24:08.072 --> 00:24:09.323
Dude.

351
00:24:12.451 --> 00:24:13.911
Huh?

352
00:24:27.633 --> 00:24:30.094
Dr. Anna Ripley.

353
00:24:31.596 --> 00:24:34.015
Why am I not surprised. Percival?

354
00:24:34.098 --> 00:24:37.226
Then again. you put things together
faster than anyone I've met.

355
00:24:37.310 --> 00:24:40.688
Hand over the vestige.
and I may let you live.

356
00:24:40.771 --> 00:24:42.732
Which one?

357
00:24:44.317 --> 00:24:47.653
Mythcarver was quite handy
before you stole it back.

358
00:24:48.654 --> 00:24:52.408
Ah. you've improved my old prototype.

359
00:24:52.491 --> 00:24:53.701
How flattering.

360
00:24:53.784 --> 00:24:55.661
There's nowhere to run. Ripley.

361
00:24:55.745 --> 00:24:57.413
You're all alone.

362
00:24:57.496 --> 00:24:59.832
Oh. that's the thing. Percival.

363
00:24:59.916 --> 00:25:02.793
I'm never alone.

364
00:25:08.341 --> 00:25:11.677
We had a bargain. Percy.

365
00:25:11.761 --> 00:25:15.765
And I will happily collect.

366
00:25:40.289 --> 00:25:42.375
<i>♪ Do ya spice? ♪</i>

367
00:25:42.458 --> 00:25:46.212
<i>♪ Oh. ah. gotcha. unh! ♪</i>

368
00:25:46.295 --> 00:25:48.464
<i>♪ You wanna spice? ♪</i>

369
00:25:48.547 --> 00:25:50.716
<i>♪ Sexy mama ♪</i>

370
00:25:50.800 --> 00:25:53.844
<i>♪ Oh. get nice with me and spice ♪♪</i>

371
00:26:15.324 --> 00:26:17.285
Chirp.
